# Themezur Post–Header/Footer Roadmap

Build in this order. Do not skip ahead unless the user asks.

## Phase 1 — Blog Archive + Single

- [x] Themezur blog mode vs Hello default
- [x] Archive: grid/list, columns, meta, excerpt, read more, pagination
- [x] Single post: image, meta, tags, author box, prev/next, related, comments
- [x] Panel tab + Help docs

## Phase 2 — Global design tokens

- [x] Expanded color + typography + radius + container + button tokens
- [x] `:root` CSS variables + `design.css` base application
- [x] General panel controls + Help docs

## Phase 3 — 404 + Search results

- [x] Native 404 + search templates
- [x] Panel tab + Help docs

## Phase 4 — WooCommerce shop templates

- [x] Shop columns / per page / card style / catalog tools
- [x] Related & upsells counts
- [x] Token-based CSS polish + panel + Help docs

## Phase 5 — Advanced WooCommerce storefront

Template strategy: hooks + CSS + tiny partials (no full WC template copies). Fast assets only on matching pages.

### 5A — Single product (PDP)

- [x] Layouts: classic / gallery_wide / stacked (body class + CSS)
- [x] Sale % badge, rating / SKU / stock toggles
- [x] Sticky add-to-cart bar (desktop, product-only JS)
- [x] Trust / shipping note
- [x] Related / upsells show + counts
- [x] Panel + Help docs

### 5B — Shop archive depth

- [x] Sale % (via single toggle) / New badges on cards, hover 2nd image
- [x] Loop AJAX ATC polish + optional YITH wishlist on card
- [x] Shop sidebar widget area + left/right/none layout
- [x] Mobile filter drawer (widget content, not custom AJAX filters)
- [x] Panel + Help docs

### 5C — Mini-cart + Cart / Checkout

- [x] Mini-cart drawer via WC fragments + qty AJAX
- [x] Cart / checkout token polish (hooks + CSS, no full template copies)
- [x] Panel + Help docs

### 5D — My Account

- [x] Dashboard / forms / orders token polish
- [x] Density option (comfortable / compact)
- [x] Panel + Help docs

## Status

Phases 1–5 complete (including advanced WooCommerce 5A–5D). Iterate from user feedback next.

## Rules

- Every feature: Themezur admin controls + Help/Docs entry
- Single `themezur_options` option
- Alpine admin only; frontend vanilla/light
- Respect Elementor Theme Builder locations when present
